  "question": {
    "text": "Choose the correct statement(s) among the following:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "dfKSS",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup></math> has tetrahedral geometry.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dRaYj",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup></math> has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> geometrical isomers.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "foYj3",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup></math> has higher spin-only magnetic moment than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OhiIH",
      "text": "The cobalt ion in<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup></math>has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridization.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup></math></p><p>Oxidation number of Fe atom <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>→</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/92c25021-1832-4cc5-8a4e-5c56de1be509-image.png\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup></math> is having tetrahedral geometry</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup></math> have three geometrical isomers.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/3529f58a-c72c-42b0-8d80-ca456514ae59-image.png\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridized with 5 -unpaired electrons. While <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>hybridised with zero unpaired electrons.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>)</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridization.</p>",
